# Stage2: Visual Reinforcement of Key Insights for Fashion Category

Based on the Stage1 analysis, we have identified the most profitable customer profiles for the Fashion category. This document presents visual evidence to reinforce those conclusions, helping merchants focus their marketing efforts effectively.

## 1. Profit by Customer Segment

![Profit by Customer Segment](profit_by_segment.png)

The Consumer segment contributes the highest total profit (86.2M USD), followed by Corporate (50.7M USD) and Home Office (30.4M USD). This highlights that individual consumers are the most lucrative customer group within Fashion, suggesting that marketing campaigns should prioritize this segment.

## 2. Profit by Gender

![Profit by Gender](profit_by_gender.png)

Female customers generate about 92.0M USD in profit, compared to 75.3M USD from male customers. While both genders are valuable, the higher absolute profit from females indicates a stronger revenue stream and potential for further engagement.

## 3. Profit by Region (Top 10)

![Profit by Region (Top 10)](profit_by_region.png)

Central region leads with 35.4M USD, followed by South (21.2M USD) and North (17.3M USD). These top three regions account for more than half of the total profit. Geographic targeting in these high-performing regions can yield the greatest return on investment.

## 4. Profit by Age Group

![Profit by Age Group](profit_by_age.png)

Customers aged 20–29 generate the highest profit (75.8M USD), which is almost double that of the next age group (30–39, 38.3M USD). The youth demographic dominates Fashion spending, reinforcing the need for age-appropriate product designs and digital-first marketing.

## 5. Browsing Engagement vs Profit

![Browsing Time vs Profit](browse_vs_profit.png)

A strong positive correlation (0.905) exists between total browsing time and total profit per customer. This suggests that customers who spend more time exploring Fashion products tend to make larger purchases. Enhancing user experience to encourage longer browsing sessions can directly boost profitability.

## Summary

The visualizations confirm that the most profitable user profile for the Fashion category is: **Consumer segment, female, aged 20–29, located in the Central region, and exhibiting high browsing engagement**. Merchants should tailor their strategies to this profile while also maintaining a balanced approach to other segments that show significant profit potential.
```)

