[1;33m[2026-03-03 18:36:04,446 [31mINFO [32magents/221-MainProcess[1;33m] [0mObservation: # Stage 1: Analysis of Annual Profit Margin Fluctuations and RFM Segmentation

## 1. Annual Profit Margin by Product Category (2022–2024)

We first calculated the profit margin (profit ÷ sales) for each product category per year.

| Product Category | 2022 Margin | 2023 Margin | 2024 Margin |
|------------------|-------------|-------------|-------------|
| Auto & Accessories | 44.01% | 44.24% | 44.18% |
| Electronic        | 44.31% | 44.02% | 44.04% |
| **Home & Furniture** | **44.43%** | **44.97%** | **44.20%** |
| Fashion           | 47.71% | 47.62% | 47.64% |

The **Home & Furniture** category exhibited the largest swing (max–min) of **0.77 percentage points**, slightly larger than the swings observed in other categories (Auto & Accessories 0.23 pp, Electronic 0.29 pp, Fashion 0.10 pp). This makes it the category of interest for further analysis.

## 2. Drivers of Margin Volatility for Home & Furniture

### 2.1 Product‑Mix Shift
Within Home & Furniture, the sales composition changed between 2023 and 2024:

- **High‑margin products** (Towels, Sofa Covers, Bed Sheets) declined from 52.6% of segment sales in 2023 to 51.5% in 2024 for the core (High RFM) segment.
- **Low‑margin products** (e.g., Dinner Crockery, Dinning Tables) increased their share.

This shift toward lower‑margin items contributed to the overall margin dip in 2024.

### 2.2 Pricing & Cost Indicators
- Average discount rose from 2.99% in 2022 to 3.02% in 2024 for the whole category.
- Average shipping cost fell from $5.72 to $5.60, but the cost reduction did not fully offset the discount increase.
- Order‑priority distribution remained stable (Second Class accounts for 100% of shipments), so shipping method was not a driver.
