|--------------|-----------|--------------|-------------------------|---------------|
| Consumer     | 409       | $1,271,091.90| $3,107.80              | 24.2%         |
| Corporate    | 238       | $  753,602.70| $3,166.40              | 26.5%         |
| Home Office  | 148       | $  459,260.60| $3,103.11              | 25.0%         |

**Insight:** Corporate customers yield the highest average profit per customer and have the largest proportion of high‑value customers.

## 3. Demographic Breakdown

### 3.1 Gender
| Gender | Customers | Total Profit | Avg Profit per Customer | High‑Value % |
|--------|-----------|--------------|-------------------------|---------------|
| Female | 405       | $1,366,498.50| $3,374.07              | 31.6%         |
| Male   | 390       | $1,117,456.70| $2,865.27              | 18.2%         |

**Insight:** Female customers generate ~18% more profit per customer and are 1.7× more likely to be high‑value than male customers.

### 3.2 Age Group
| Age Group | Customers | Total Profit | Avg Profit per Customer | High‑Value % |
|-----------|-----------|--------------|-------------------------|---------------|
| <20       | 118       | $  372,944.70| $3,160.55              | 25.4%         |
| 20‑30     | 351       | $1,091,027.90| $3,108.34              | 25.6%         |
| 30‑40     | 167       | $  522,418.90| $3,128.26              | 24.0%         |
| 40‑50     | 91        | $  278,765.10| $3,063.35              | 20.9%         |
| 50‑60     | 39        | $  125,713.20| $3,223.42              | 28.2%         |
| 60+       | 29        | $   93,085.40| $3,209.84              | **31.0%**     |

**Insight:** Customers aged 50‑60 and 60+ show the highest average profit and the highest likelihood of being high‑value. The 20‑30 age group contributes the largest total profit because of its size.

### 3.3 Education Level
| Education Level   | Customers | Total Profit | Avg Profit per Customer | High‑Value % |
|-------------------|-----------|--------------|-------------------------|---------------|
| High School       | 160       | $  520,672.90| $3,254.21              | **31.9%**     |
