The latest date is 2025-06-21. So last 30 days would be from 2025-05-22 to 2025-06-21. Need to compute growth rate of CAC (customer_acquisition_cost) over that period, and compare LTV/CAC ratio.

But we need to identify campaigns that have been running >120 days. We'll need to know campaign start date. In customer_acquisition_analysis, we have `acquisition_cohort` which is maybe the cohort start date (first conversion date?). That could be used to compute days running per campaign? Not exactly.

Maybe we need to join the tables on account_id and advertising_channel_type and date_day to get campaign-level CAC and LTV/CAC. However there is no guarantee of direct mapping. Let's explore distinct combination in customer_acquisition_analysis that might represent campaigns.

