From summary stats, low-margin orders have much lower Sales Quantity (mean 6.7 vs 53.2) and lower Total Logistics Revenue (98.3 vs 1482). Their Freight Cost is higher (63.3 vs 54.4) and Warehousing Cost higher (29.7 vs 27.5). Discount Amount slightly higher (10.14 vs 9.99). Also low-margin group has negative average Profit Margin (-0.667) vs positive (0.902). So low-margin orders are small orders with high per-unit costs, possibly due to fixed costs spread over fewer items.

Need to compute per-unit costs: freight per unit, warehousing per unit, etc. Let's compute cost per unit (Sales Quantity). We'll add columns.

